    <h1 class="section__heading">Privacy policy</h1>
    <p>Last updated 8 October 2026.</p>

    <h2>Who we are</h2>
    <p>Layton Unlocked (laytonunlocked.com) is a community initiative that shares events, activities and local support in Layton, Blackpool. It is run by Adam Turnbull. If you have any questions about this policy or your information, email <a href="mailto:adam@laytonunlocked.com">adam@laytonunlocked.com</a>.</p>

    <h2>What we collect and why</h2>
    <p><strong>Newsletter (the Layton Loop).</strong> If you sign up, we collect your email address so we can send you events, activities and community news. We only do this with your consent, which you give by ticking the box on the form. Your email address is stored by our email provider, Brevo. We keep it until you unsubscribe, and every email includes an unsubscribe link.</p>
    <p><strong>"What's missing in Layton" survey.</strong> When you pick an answer, we add one to a running total for that answer. We do not collect your name, email address or any other detail, so your answer is anonymous. We save a note in your browser so the pop-up does not keep appearing.</p>
    <p><strong>Analytics (only if you accept).</strong> If you click Accept on the cookie banner, we use Google Analytics to count visits and see which pages people use. It records things like the pages you view, roughly where you are, and the device and browser you use. We use this only to improve the site. If you click Decline, Google Analytics is not loaded at all.</p>
    <p><strong>Hosting.</strong> The site is delivered by Cloudflare, which processes your IP address and basic request details to serve pages and keep the site secure.</p>
    <p><strong>Fonts.</strong> The site loads its fonts from Google Fonts, which means your browser contacts Google when a page loads.</p>
    <p><strong>Emails you send us.</strong> If you email us, we keep your message and address so we can reply.</p>

    <h2>Cookies and similar storage</h2>
    <table>
      <thead><tr><th>Name</th><th>Purpose</th><th>Lasts</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><td>lu_consent</td><td>Remembers your cookie choice (stored in your browser)</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
        <tr><td>lu_survey_done</td><td>Remembers you have seen the survey pop-up (stored in your browser)</td><td>Until you clear it</td></tr>
